[{:db/id "q-102558/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "a7649319-8d95-5cf4-b3c7-6c62ca0bbfa6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-102558/selection/ae9425c9e204310ed598f729a242e0b42a2acbbf125bff30bc2080e10b8cf473" :answer/id #uuid "54874472-e059-576e-a4f3-011d082adcd1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-102558/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer/id #uuid "efd40b21-153e-56ff-b343-99c8aac2ae03" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-102558/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "89024da1-983c-5a3e-9382-e416645cfce8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-102558/selection/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" :answer/id #uuid "8109e3e0-f7d9-51f0-820e-694823ad001c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-102558/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "3f38c4c5-e246-5b02-b089-0d899df8b262" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-102558/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer-field/choices ["q-102558/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" "q-102558/selection/ae9425c9e204310ed598f729a242e0b42a2acbbf125bff30bc2080e10b8cf473" "q-102558/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" "q-102558/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" "q-102558/selection/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-102558" :question/id #uuid "fe474dc6-fd17-55a5-b177-03917c5838c0" :question/math-academy-id "q-102558" :question/problem "Given that \n\n$$\n\\frac{5{x}^{2}-5x+17}{({x}^{2}+5)(x-2)}=\\frac{Ax-1}{{x}^{2}+5}+\\frac{3}{x-2},\n$$\n\nwhat is the value of $A?$" :question/worked-solution "Multiplying both sides of the given equality by $({x}^{2}+5)(x-2)$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5{x}^{2}-5x+17 & =(Ax-1)(x-2)+3({x}^{2}+5).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLetting $x=1$  gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5(1)^{2}-5(1)+17 & =(A(1)-1)(1-2)+3({1}^{2}+5) \\\\ 17 & =(A-1)(-1)+3(6) \\\\ 17 & =-A+1+18 \\\\ -2 & =-A \\\\ A & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-102558/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5c6490a5-4923-58e8-99c3-d568a033800e"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-102558"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-49718"] :question/problem "Given that\n\n$$\n\\frac{5}{({x}^{2}+1)(x+2)}=\\frac{Ax+B}{{x}^{2}+1}+\\frac{C}{x+2},\n$$\n\nwhere $A,$ $B$ and $C$ are real constants, determine the value of $A+B+C.$" :question/worked-solution "We multiply both sides of the given equality by $({x}^{2}+1)(x+2)$ and get\n\n$$\n5=(Ax+B)(x+2)+C({x}^{2}+1).\n$$\n\nPlugging in $x=-2$ eliminates the $A$ and $B$ terms and allows us to solve for $C.$ We get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5 & =(A(-2)+B)(-2+2)+C((-2)^{2}+1) \\\\ 5 & =5C \\\\ C & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nPlugging in $x=0$ eliminates the $A$ term, and using our result for $C$ allows us to solve for $B.$ We get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5 & =(A(0)+B)(0+2)+(1)({0}^{2}+1) \\\\ 5 & =2B+1 \\\\ 2B & =4 \\\\ B & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, to solve for $A,$ we choose $x=1$ and use our results for $B$ and $C.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5 & =(A(1)+2)(1+2)+1({1}^{2}+1) \\\\ 5 & =(A+2)(3)+2 \\\\ 3A+6 & =3 \\\\ 3A & =-3 \\\\ A & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo we have $A=-1,B=2,$ and $C=1.$ Therefore, our final result is\n\n$$\nA+B+C=-1+2+1=2.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-51144/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "f986a5ea-d071-57cf-a4dd-b02f6efd7ef4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-51144/selection/d027d90726f5bdbf1525aade1b6bde5c85e2082f2b792dfacee399fcc90e9833" :answer/id #uuid "45184ff8-36be-5a4d-b943-eca88602e81d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-51144/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "a0cf693c-dc1c-5acc-a3b9-4558015a1ae9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-51144/selection/371b27a4bfd1234e92f61a2867afaaf09c5edc704595b0d22c8f115a87d5b89a" :answer/id #uuid "1feeb5e3-45f2-51a1-a3f6-6472b88c2415" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{9}{7}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-51144/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer/id #uuid "47ab84c3-7d44-5521-bbaf-6c183cc4d8ad" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-51144/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "0dc0a31f-af8c-5a9c-bd61-5eb0c29636f2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-51144/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer-field/choices ["q-51144/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" "q-51144/selection/d027d90726f5bdbf1525aade1b6bde5c85e2082f2b792dfacee399fcc90e9833" "q-51144/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" "q-51144/selection/371b27a4bfd1234e92f61a2867afaaf09c5edc704595b0d22c8f115a87d5b89a" "q-51144/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-51144" :question/id #uuid "e9e48716-0b82-59b0-97d7-83aff7e756a9" :question/math-academy-id "q-51144" :question/problem "Given that \n\n$$\n\\frac{5{x}^{2}+x+3}{({x}^{2}+1)x}=\\frac{Ax+1}{{x}^{2}+1}+\\frac{3}{x},\n$$\n\nwhat is the value of $A?$" :question/worked-solution "Multiplying both sides of the given equality by $({x}^{2}+1)x$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5{x}^{2}+x+3 & =(Ax+1)x+3({x}^{2}+1).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLetting $x=1$  gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5(1)^{2}+1+3 & =(A(1)+1)(1)+3({1}^{2}+1) \\\\ 9 & =(A+1)+3(2) \\\\ 9 & =A+1+6 \\\\ A & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-51144/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5c6490a5-4923-58e8-99c3-d568a033800e"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-51144"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-102575/selection/ec291518075c8afd61e132b4b63ae7b8c5c3161fa02672c38077460c3dc0ec45" :answer/id #uuid "2a79315d-acb8-5a84-bf21-49c8b9b0ab8b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2x+3}{({x}^{2}+x+3)}+\\frac{1}{(x-4)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-102575/selection/3724d2d205b8dd66843b5f91d949e4a51f6aaa618061bcded8e3c57c3a09cd31" :answer/id #uuid "66ceff31-4de7-5e73-b8f4-617aa95482fa" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3x+1}{({x}^{2}+x+3)}+\\frac{3}{(x-4)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-102575/selection/66eb7dd5c7a508f53a4535b2afecdecdee255de7a48f9a991b9f45c359dbec94" :answer/id #uuid "4d2129c9-cfa0-5852-ad60-250f0f96e996" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2x+1}{({x}^{2}+x+3)}-\\frac{5}{(x-4)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-102575/selection/e38cc788cc55dd0eb904350ab309daf92e0eacbf34b553ea4597543e8374f8a3" :answer/id #uuid "c7cdb026-7732-59a5-8b47-371bd541f5f2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{x-2}{({x}^{2}+x+3)}+\\frac{3}{(x-4)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-102575/selection/5fbf2cbe328ea788f2d50e0957abc0a5ec51916b62e5cf367e452ff2c2396e1a" :answer/id #uuid "7e17cec5-946b-57b3-93d6-a53a3fbfec68" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3x+4}{({x}^{2}+x+3)}+\\frac{1}{(x-4)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-102575/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "050ca3e5-da3e-5612-80f8-6609b89f3e54" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-102575/selection/3724d2d205b8dd66843b5f91d949e4a51f6aaa618061bcded8e3c57c3a09cd31" :answer-field/choices ["q-102575/selection/ec291518075c8afd61e132b4b63ae7b8c5c3161fa02672c38077460c3dc0ec45" "q-102575/selection/3724d2d205b8dd66843b5f91d949e4a51f6aaa618061bcded8e3c57c3a09cd31" "q-102575/selection/66eb7dd5c7a508f53a4535b2afecdecdee255de7a48f9a991b9f45c359dbec94" "q-102575/selection/e38cc788cc55dd0eb904350ab309daf92e0eacbf34b553ea4597543e8374f8a3" "q-102575/selection/5fbf2cbe328ea788f2d50e0957abc0a5ec51916b62e5cf367e452ff2c2396e1a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-102575" :question/id #uuid "521a4105-19cc-5686-bb26-dc951626ae6d" :question/math-academy-id "q-102575" :question/problem "Express $\\frac{6{x}^{2}-8x+5}{({x}^{2}+x+3)(x-4)}$ as a sum of partial fractions." :question/worked-solution "Our task is to find $A,$ $B,$ and $C$ such that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{6{x}^{2}-8x+5}{({x}^{2}+x+3)(x-4)} & =\\frac{Ax+B}{({x}^{2}+x+3)}+\\frac{C}{(x-4)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that since ${x}^{2}+2x+3$ is an irreducible quadratic factor, we must use a linear term $Ax+B$ in the numerator.\n\nWe multiply both sides by $({x}^{2}+x+3)(x-4)$ and get\n\n$$\n6{x}^{2}-8x+5=(Ax+B)(x-4)+C({x}^{2}+x+3).\n$$\n\nPlugging in $x=4$ eliminates the $A$ and $B$ terms and allows us to solve for $C.$ We get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6(4)^{2}-8(4)+5 & =(A(4)+B)(4-4)+C({4}^{2}+4+3) \\\\ 69 & =23C \\\\ C & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nPlugging in $x=0$ eliminates the $A$ term, and using our result for $C$ allows us to solve for $B.$ We get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6(0)^{2}-8(0)+5 & =(A(0)+B)(0-4)+C({0}^{2}+0+3) \\\\ 5 & =-4B+3C \\\\ 5 & =-4B+3(3) \\\\ 4B & =9-5 \\\\ B & =\\frac{4}{4} \\\\ B & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, to solve for $A,$ we choose $x=1$ and use our results for $B$ and $C.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6(1)^{2}-8(1)+5 & =(A(1)+B)(1-4)+C({1}^{2}+1+3) \\\\ 3 & =-3A-3B+5C \\\\ 3 & =-3A-3(1)+5(3) \\\\ 3 & =-3A-3+15 \\\\ 3A & =-3-3+15 \\\\ A & =\\frac{9}{3} \\\\ A & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo we have $A=3,B=1,$ and $C=3.$ Therefore, our final result is\n\n$$\n\\frac{6{x}^{2}-8x+5}{({x}^{2}+x+3)(x-4)}=\\frac{3x+1}{({x}^{2}+x+3)}+\\frac{3}{(x-4)}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-102575/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d10c4317-f4b3-5846-8376-c7d382fc0ba3"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-102575"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-4046"] :question/problem "Given that \n\n$$\n\\dfrac{7 x^2 - 2x - 13 }{(x^2+1)(x+1) } = \\dfrac{9x+B}{ x^2 +1} - \\dfrac{2}{x+1} ,\n$$\n\nwhat is the value of $B?$" :question/worked-solution "Multiplying both sides of the given equality by $(x^2+1)(x+1)$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}7{x}^{2}-2x-13 & =(9x+B)(x+1)-2({x}^{2}+1).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLetting $x=0$  gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}7(0)^{2}-2(0)-13 & =(9\\cdot (0)+B)(0+1)-2((0)^{2}+1) \\\\ -13 & =B-2 \\\\ B & =-11.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-504"] :question/worked-solution "Our task is to find $A,$ $B$ and $C$ such that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2x+3}{({x}^{2}+4)(x-1)} & =\\frac{Ax+B}{{x}^{2}+4}+\\frac{C}{x-1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that since $x^2+4$ is an irreducible quadratic factor, we must use a linear term $Ax+B$ in the numerator.\n\nWe multiply both sides by $(x^2+4)(x-1)$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x+3 & =(Ax+B)(x-1)+C({x}^{2}+4).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nPlugging in $x=1$ eliminates the $A$ and $B$ terms and allows us to solve for $C.$ We get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2(1)+3 & =(A(1)+B)(1-1)+C({1}^{2}+4) \\\\ 5 & =5C \\\\ C & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nPlugging in $x=0$ eliminates the $A$ term, and using our result for $C$ allows us to solve for $B.$ We get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2(0)+3 & =(A(0)+B)(0-1)+C({0}^{2}+4) \\\\ 3 & =-B+4C \\\\ 3 & =-B+4(1) \\\\ B & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, to solve for $A,$ we choose $x=2$ and use our results for $B$ and $C.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2(2)+3 & =(A(2)+B)(2-1)+C({2}^{2}+4) \\\\ 7 & =2A+B+8C \\\\ 7 & =2A+1+8(1) \\\\ 2A & =-2 \\\\ A & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo we have $A=-1,$ $B=1,$ and $C=1.$ Therefore, our final result is\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{2x+3}{(x^2+4)(x-1)} = \\dfrac{1-x}{x^2+4} +\\dfrac{1}{x-1}.\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]}]
